# =============================================================================
# What never gets committed, and why. Everything under raw_input_data/ and
# data_prep/*/output/ is ignored by default; each block below excepts only
# the specific files confirmed to be small, aggregate, non-identifiable
# summary statistics (SNP/allele-level, not participant-level). If you add a
# new data_prep/ output and aren't sure whether it's safe to except, don't -
# leave it ignored and ask first. See DATA_ACCESS.md for the public-facing
# explanation of what's included/excluded and why.
# =============================================================================

# --- raw_input_data/: every private input file, entirely ---
# Participant phenotypes, diagnoses, genotypes/dosages, HLA imputation calls,
# neuropathology/microglia measurements - see raw_input_data/README.txt and
# SOURCE_DATA_MANIFEST.md. data_paths.R.example is a placeholder-only
# template (no real paths or data), safe to publish.
!raw_input_data/
raw_input_data/*
!raw_input_data/data_paths.R.example

# --- data_prep/*/output/: pipeline working directories ---
# Ignored by default because most of what lands here is one of:
#   - participant IDs (e.g. study_cohort_samples.txt) - directly re-identifying
#   - individual-level data (one row per participant) - phenotypes, dosages,
#     neuropathology/microglia measurements, even after merging
#   - large regenerable intermediates (PLINK/GCTA working files, full
#     genotype exports, up to several GB)
# Exceptions below are the opposite of all three: small, aggregate,
# SNP/allele-level summary statistics with no participant-level rows,
# verified by inspecting each file's actual header before excepting it here.
data_prep/*/output/*

!data_prep/study_cohort_genetics/output/clumping_r2_080.clumps
!data_prep/study_cohort_genetics/output/cojo_haplotypes_minor_allele.csv
!data_prep/study_cohort_genetics/output/hla_alleles_snps_regression.csv
!data_prep/nbb_replication_cohort/output/microglia_neuropathology_regression.csv

!data_prep/study_cohort_genetics/output/haplotype_ld/
data_prep/study_cohort_genetics/output/haplotype_ld/*
!data_prep/study_cohort_genetics/output/haplotype_ld/hla_alleles_snps_ld_matrix.ld
!data_prep/study_cohort_genetics/output/haplotype_ld/hla_alleles_snps_ld_matrix.bim

!data_prep/study_cohort_genetics/output/regional_ld/
data_prep/study_cohort_genetics/output/regional_ld/*
!data_prep/study_cohort_genetics/output/regional_ld/regional_ld_pairs.ld

# Explicitly NOT excepted (never committed), despite being read directly by a
# script - flagged here so it's unmistakable, not just covered by the blanket
# rule above:
#   - data_prep/study_cohort_genetics/output/study_cohort_samples.txt
#     Raw participant ID list (from 1_clumping_cojo.R, read by 2_regional_ld.R).
#     Directly re-identifying - never share this file, in any form.
#   - data_prep/100plus_study_cohort/output/hla_alleles_snps_dosages_microglia_neuropathology_100plus.csv
#   - data_prep/nbb_replication_cohort/output/hla_alleles_snps_dosages_neuropathology_nbb.csv
#     Individual-level (one row per participant), not aggregate summary
#     statistics, even though read directly by
#     data_prep/nbb_replication_cohort/3_microglia_neuropathology_regression.R.
#     Re-running that script needs data_prep/ re-run locally with real data
#     access - see DATA_ACCESS.md. A placeholder README.md is committed in
#     their place so these folders still appear on GitHub, explaining why
#     they're empty.
!data_prep/100plus_study_cohort/output/README.md
!data_prep/nbb_replication_cohort/output/README.md

# --- Manuscript working files dropped at the repo root ---
# Draft manuscript and supplementary tables, kept here for local
# cross-referencing against the code - not part of the code repository itself
# and never committed. Publish the manuscript through the journal/preprint,
# not this repo.
*.docx
tables_1_2_3_supplementary_tables_1_2.xlsx
